sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/darwin1859-ch04-03> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>;
    dc:description "No country's native inhabitants are so perfectly adapted that none could be improved, as shown by introduced species having established firmly in every country.";
    dc:type "empirical-generalization";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "No native biota is so well adapted that it cannot be improved";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "Charles Darwin, On the Origin of Species (1st ed., London: John Murray, 1859), Chapter IV, “Natural Selection”; section “Natural Selection: its power compared with man’s selection, its power on characters of trifling importance, its power at all ages and on both sexes”. Scope: native biotas of all countries and regions"
}
